import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 499 | Cross-IP Synthesis: The Universality of the Law-First Axiom — Why Every IP Needs Law to Precede","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 499 | Cross-IP Synthesis: The Universality of the Law-First Axiom — Why Every IP Needs Law to Precede","no":499,"module":2,"tags":["Cross-IP Synthesis","Law-First Axiom","Universality","Setting Self-Consistency","Never Retcon"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis","14-Unified Cultivation-Realm Division","10-300-Origin Cultivation-System Overview"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0499_模块2-跨IP综合-法则优先公理的普适性-为何所有IP都需要法则先行.md","filePath":"en/0499_模块2-跨IP综合-法则优先公理的普适性-为何所有IP都需要法则先行.md"}'),a={name:"en/0499_模块2-跨IP综合-法则优先公理的普适性-为何所有IP都需要法则先行.md"};function n(r,e,l,h,u,c){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="entry-499-cross-ip-synthesis-the-universality-of-the-law-first-axiom-—-why-every-ip-needs-law-to-precede" tabindex="-1">Entry 499 | Cross-IP Synthesis: The Universality of the Law-First Axiom — Why Every IP Needs Law to Precede <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-499-cross-ip-synthesis-the-universality-of-the-law-first-axiom-—-why-every-ip-needs-law-to-precede" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 499 | Cross-IP Synthesis: The Universality of the Law-First Axiom — Why Every IP Needs Law to Precede&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Cross-IP Synthesis (Entry 8) | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 14, 10</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-law-first-is-the-common-prescription-for-all-cosmoses" tabindex="-1">Introduction: law first is the common prescription for all cosmoses <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-law-first-is-the-common-prescription-for-all-cosmoses" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: law first is the common prescription for all cosmoses&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou (Myriad-Spirits Balanced-Anchor Origin Universe)&#39;s six top-level axioms — anti-predation axiom, republican axiom of Myriad Races, collective ascension axiom, causal self-discipline axiom, <strong>law-first axiom</strong>, universal equal infinite law as core — among which the law-first axiom is the meta-axiom cutting across all problems. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. This entry argues: why Tang Luo, Shrouding, Douluo, Desolation Era, Dragon Ball, Infinite Terror, Jackie Chan Adventures, Dragon Rune — all IPs&#39; final root cause is &quot;law not first&quot;; all IPs&#39; prescription is &quot;law first.&quot;</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-cross-ip-summary" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Cross-IP Summary) <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-cross-ip-summary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Cross-IP Summary)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Cosmoses where law does not precede have a common feature in energy waste: <strong>rules drift with the plot.</strong> Tang Luo&#39;s rules tied to himself; Ye Fan&#39;s rules tied to Great Emperor; Dragon Ball&#39;s rules lifted with transformations; Infinite Terror&#39;s rules rewritten with the box; Dragon Rune&#39;s rules inflated with Gu Chensha. Rules unstable, civilization cannot plan, energy cannot sediment.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-cross-ip-summary" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Cross-IP Summary) <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-cross-ip-summary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Cross-IP Summary)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A world that casually changes rules is not worth building for. Because you do not know whether what you build today will be erased by new rules tomorrow. <strong>Law not first is the deepest root of civilizational regression.</strong></p><h2 id="iii-universality-argument-for-the-law-first-axiom" tabindex="-1">III. Universality Argument for the Law-First Axiom <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-universality-argument-for-the-law-first-axiom" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Universality Argument for the Law-First Axiom&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Why does the law-first axiom apply to all IPs? Because it resolves the structural contradiction of all long-form narratives: <strong>plot needs to develop; setting needs to be stable.</strong> When the two conflict, who yields?</p><ul><li>Predatory IP: plot does not yield; setting yields → retcon, inflation, bad ending</li><li>Heng Yuan Zhou: setting does not yield; plot yields → law anchored; never bloats</li></ul><p>Tang Luo, Ye Fan, Shi Hao, Ji Ning, Wukong, Zheng Zha, Jackie Chan, Gu Chensha — all their problems can ultimately be summarized in one sentence: <strong>law did not precede, so plot kidnapped setting.</strong> As long as law is established in front, all problems solved.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Not-First</th><th>Law-First</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Realms lifted with protagonist</td><td>Nine-plus-two realms fixed</td></tr><tr><td>Rules changed with plot</td><td>Law anchored; revisions go legislation</td></tr><tr><td>New setting overturns old setting</td><td>New dimensions go appendix; do not overturn</td></tr><tr><td>Protagonist halo bottom-line</td><td>Plane-Transcendent four-dimensional exam</td></tr><tr><td>Never-retcon depends on author conscience</td><td>Never-retcon written into constitution</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Quest Sediment Domain runs &quot;law-first transformation&quot; for all eight IPs: freeze each IP&#39;s early rules as baseline law; subsequent plot must be deduced within the law. Result: all IPs&#39; self-consistency rises from &quot;medium-low / low&quot; to &quot;high&quot;; retcon risk drops from &quot;high / extremely high&quot; to &quot;low.&quot; <strong>Law first is a universal prescription, not Heng Yuan Zhou exclusive.</strong></p><p>The reason law first is universal is that it resolves the structural contradiction of all long-form narratives — not some IP&#39;s special problem, but &quot;long-form&quot; itself&#39;s internal contradiction. Any long-form narrative must face the tension of &quot;plot must develop; setting must be stable.&quot; Short works can rely on author conscience to maintain stability, but the longer the long-form work, the more unreliable author conscience becomes — the only reliable way is to establish law at the very front, letting the law itself become the constraint. Heng Yuan Zhou did not invent a new cosmos; it only wrote the rules long-form cosmoses should have followed at the very front.</p><p>The law-first axiom&#39;s universality can also be argued from reader psychology: readers reading long-form expect to &quot;travel in a credible world.&quot; A credible world must have credible rules. If rules change with plot, readers cannot trust this world — they no longer care about the protagonist&#39;s fate, because they know the protagonist&#39;s fate is arbitrarily arranged by the author. Law first is protecting reader trust. <strong>Reader trust is the most precious asset of a long-form cosmos.</strong> Douluo, Shrouding, Dragon Ball, Infinite Terror, Dragon Rune&#39;s late collapse is not because they wrote poorly, but because they overdraw reader trust. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s law-first axiom is to preserve this trust.</p><p>The law-first axiom&#39;s universality can ultimately be summarized in one sentence: <strong>all long-form cosmoses&#39; root cause is the same — law not first.</strong> All long-form cosmoses&#39; prescription is also the same — law first. Douluo, Shrouding, Dragon Ball, Infinite Terror, Jackie Chan Adventures, Dragon Rune, all fall ill from the same cause, all recover from the same medicine. Heng Yuan Zhou did not invent a new cosmos; it only wrote all long-form cosmoses&#39; original rules at the very front.</p><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Self-consistency law</strong>: the more law precedes, the higher the self-consistency</li><li><strong>Retcon risk law</strong>: the more law precedes, the lower the retcon risk</li><li><strong>Heng Yuan Zhou reference</strong>: the extreme model of law first</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: law first; early setting not zeroed by late</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: law public; not privately hoarded by protagonist</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo did not explicitly legislate; law tied to himself</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: law public; Myriad Ranks can plan according to law</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: law first; cosmos can infinitely expand without collapse</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The law-first axiom is not Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s private doctrine; it is the public prescription for all long-form cosmoses. <strong>Why does every IP need law first? Because as long as law does not precede, plot kidnaps setting; setting kidnaps readers; readers vote with their feet.</strong> Heng Yuan Zhou only did this one thing right — law established at the very front; then all other axioms have somewhere to rest.</p><p>In the final analysis, Cross-IP synthesis · universality of the law-first axiom · why every IP needs law to precede described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./494_模块2-跨IP综合-吃书烂尾根源总分析-剧情绑架设定的五种形态.html">Entry 494 · Five Retcon Forms</a> · <a href="./500_模块2-模块二终章-诸天对标批判库总结-从掠夺到共生的文明跃迁.html">Entry 500 · Final Chapter</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/14-修炼境界统一划分.html">14-Unified Cultivation-Realm Division</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const g=t(a,[["render",n]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
